IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulation 28: the customer due diligence measures a relevant person applies once regulation 27 requires them.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- THE SHAPE.  Most paragraphs say what the relevant person "must" do, subject to a gate ("This regulation applies when ..."), a case
-- ("Where the customer is a body corporate") or an exception ("unless ... known to, and has been verified by"):
--  * a gate ("This regulation applies when ...") or a case ("Where the customer is a body corporate") that is not met answers JUST FALSE ("when" read as "where",
--    fork F-when; ruling 2026-11-05, (b)); a scope limit with no "only" ("ongoing monitoring of a business relationship") answers NOTHING (ruling 2026-11-05, (c));
--  * an "unless" exception that applies answers JUST FALSE (the text says no); an "if" that fails answers JUST FALSE (Marginal readings, (a));
--  * every other case answers JUST TRUE: the relevant person must do it.
-- The functions answer "must the relevant person do this on these facts?".  Whether it has done it is the compliance question of the duty
-- checklists in the other modules; here the checklist form is used only where the paragraph is about what a person has to show or take into account.
-- Where a paragraph lists what must be obtained or done, a companion function returns the list, so a seat can say what to collect.

§ `Regulation 28(1) to (2) -- When the regulation applies and the basic measures`

-- reg 28(1).  This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures.
-- SEAM S-1 (asking): regulation 27 (module mlr1-reg27-cdd-when) answers whether the relevant person is required to apply measures.
-- src:806 | (1) This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures.
@ref reg 28(1) (src:806-806)
GIVEN `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 27 has not answered whether the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures

-- reg 28(2).  The relevant person must (a) identify the customer unless the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the
-- relevant person; (b) verify the customer's identity unless the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person; and (c) assess,
-- and where appropriate obtain information on, the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship or occasional transaction.
-- src:807 | (2) The relevant person must—
-- src:808 | (a) identify the customer unless the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person;
-- src:809 | (b) verify the customer's identity unless the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person; and
-- src:810 | (c) assess, and where appropriate obtain information on, the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship or occasional transaction.
@ref reg 28(2)(a) (src:807-810)
GIVEN `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(2)(a) the relevant person must identify the customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 28(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF `the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person must— (a) identify the customer ... unless the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 28(2)(b) (src:809-809)
GIVEN `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(2)(b) the relevant person must verify the customer's identity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 28(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF `the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person must— (b) verify the customer's identity ... unless the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 28(2)(c) (src:810-810)
GIVEN `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(2)(c) the relevant person must assess the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship or occasional transaction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 28(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Regulation 28(3) to (5) -- Bodies corporate and beneficial owners`

-- reg 28(5).  Paragraphs (3)(b), (3A) and (4) do not apply where the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market.
-- src:824 | (5) Paragraphs (3)(b), (3A) and (4) do not apply where the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market.
@ref reg 28(5) (src:824-824)
GIVEN `the customer is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer's securities are listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(5) paragraphs (3)(b), (3A) and (4) do not apply to the customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the customer is a company` AND `the customer's securities are listed on a regulated market` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply where the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market"; the paragraph says nothing of another customer (Ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)

