-- reg 28(3A).  Where the customer is a legal person, trust, company, foundation or similar legal arrangement the relevant person must take reasonable
-- measures to understand the ownership and control structure of that legal person, trust, company, foundation or similar legal arrangement.
-- "Legal person" and "similar legal arrangement" are not defined in the text: the forms of customer the paragraph names (a company, a trust, a foundation
-- or other arrangement similar to a trust) answer JUST TRUE; the other forms answer NOTHING (undefined term).
-- src:819 | (3A) Where the customer is a legal person, trust, company, foundation or similar legal arrangement the relevant person must take reasonable measures to understand the ownership and control structure of that legal person, trust, company, foundation or similar legal arrangement.
@ref reg 28(3A) (src:819-819)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(3A) the form of customer is a legal person, trust, company, foundation or similar legal arrangement` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a trust` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a foundation or other legal arrangement similar to a trust` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (3A) names legal persons, trusts, companies, foundations and similar arrangements, not individuals
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "legal person" is not defined in the text
    WHEN `a body corporate of another kind` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "legal person" is not defined in the text
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "legal person" is not defined in the text
    WHEN `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "legal person" and "similar legal arrangement" are not defined in the text
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "legal person" and "similar legal arrangement" are not defined in the text
    WHEN `the estate of a deceased person in the course of administration` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "similar legal arrangement" is not defined in the text
    WHEN `another legal entity or legal arrangement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "legal person" and "similar legal arrangement" are not defined in the text

