-- reg 28(9).  Relevant persons do not satisfy their requirements under paragraph (4) by relying solely on information delivered to the registrar under any
-- enactment that requires information to be delivered to the registrar about registrable persons, registrable relevant legal entities or registrable beneficial owners.
-- src:834 | (9) Relevant persons do not satisfy their requirements under paragraph (4) by relying solely on information delivered to the registrar under any enactment that requires information to be delivered to the registrar about registrable persons, registrable relevant legal entities or registrable beneficial owners.
@ref reg 28(9) (src:834-834)
GIVEN `the relevant person relies solely on information delivered to the registrar under an enactment that requires information to be delivered to the registrar about registrable persons, registrable relevant legal entities or registrable beneficial owners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(9) the relevant person satisfies its requirements under paragraph (4)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person relies solely on information delivered to the registrar under an enactment that requires information to be delivered to the registrar about registrable persons, registrable relevant legal entities or registrable beneficial owners` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Relevant persons do not satisfy their requirements under paragraph (4) by relying solely on information delivered to the registrar"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says only that relying solely on registrar information does not satisfy paragraph (4); it does not say what does

-- reg 28(9A).  In paragraph (9): "registrable beneficial owner", "registrable person" and "registrable relevant legal entity" have the meanings given by the
-- Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 and the Companies Act 2006 (pointers outside the text); "registrar" means (i) for information delivered
-- under Part 1 of the 2022 Act, the registrar of companies for England and Wales; (ii) for information delivered under any other enactment, the registrar
-- referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006.
-- src:835 | (9A) In paragraph (9)—
-- src:836 | “registrable beneficial owner” has the meaning given in section 4(5) (application for registration) of, and Schedule 2 (registrable beneficial owners) to, the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022;
-- src:837 | “registrable person” has the meaning given in section 790C(4) (key terms) of the Companies Act 2006, including as that definition is applied under any enactment;
-- src:838 | “registrable relevant legal entity” has the meaning given in section 790C(8) of the Companies Act 2006, including as that definition is applied under any enactment;
@ref reg 28(9A) (src:835-838)
GIVEN `section 4(5) of, and Schedule 2 to, the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 answer that the individual is a registrable beneficial owner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(9A) the individual is a registrable beneficial owner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 4(5) of, and Schedule 2 to, the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 answer that the individual is a registrable beneficial owner` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `section 4(5) of, and Schedule 2 to, the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 answer that the individual is a registrable beneficial owner` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registrable beneficial owner” has the meaning given in section 4(5) ... and Schedule 2" (the Act answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by section 4(5) of, and Schedule 2 to, the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022

@ref reg 28(9A) (src:835-838)
GIVEN `section 790C(4) of the Companies Act 2006 answers that the person is a registrable person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(9A) the person is a registrable person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 790C(4) of the Companies Act 2006 answers that the person is a registrable person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `section 790C(4) of the Companies Act 2006 answers that the person is a registrable person` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registrable person” has the meaning given in section 790C(4) (key terms) of the Companies Act 2006" (the Act answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by section 790C(4) of the Companies Act 2006

@ref reg 28(9A) (src:835-838)
GIVEN `section 790C(8) of the Companies Act 2006 answers that the entity is a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(9A) the entity is a registrable relevant legal entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 790C(8) of the Companies Act 2006 answers that the entity is a registrable relevant legal entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `section 790C(8) of the Companies Act 2006 answers that the entity is a registrable relevant legal entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registrable relevant legal entity” has the meaning given in section 790C(8) of the Companies Act 2006" (the Act answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by section 790C(8) of the Companies Act 2006

DECLARE `reg 28(9A) enactment under which information is delivered` IS ONE OF
    `reg 28(9A) Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022`
    `reg 28(9A) any other enactment`

DECLARE `reg 28(9A) registrar` IS ONE OF
    `reg 28(9A) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`
    `reg 28(9A) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`

-- src:839 | “registrar” means—
-- src:840 | in relation to information delivered to the registrar under Part 1 (registration of overseas entities) of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022, the registrar of companies for England and Wales;
-- src:841 | in relation to information delivered to the registrar under any other enactment, the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) (the registrar) of the Companies Act 2006.
@ref reg 28(9A) (src:839-841)
GIVEN enactment IS A `reg 28(9A) enactment under which information is delivered`
GIVETH A `reg 28(9A) registrar`
`reg 28(9A) the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER enactment
    WHEN `reg 28(9A) Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` THEN `reg 28(9A) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`
    WHEN `reg 28(9A) any other enactment` THEN `reg 28(9A) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`

§ `Regulation 28(10) to (13) -- Agents, monitoring and risk`

-- reg 28(10).  Where a person ("A") purports to act on behalf of the customer, the relevant person must (a) verify that A is authorised to act on the
-- customer's behalf; (b) identify A; and (c) verify A's identity on the basis of documents or information in either case obtained from a reliable source
-- which is independent of both A and the customer.
-- src:842 | (10) Where a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer, the relevant person must—
-- src:843 | (a) verify that A is authorised to act on the customer's behalf;
-- src:844 | (b) identify A; and
-- src:845 | (c) verify A's identity on the basis of documents or information in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of both A and the customer.
@ref reg 28(10) (src:842-845)
GIVEN `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(10) the relevant person must verify A's authority, identify A and verify A's identity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 28(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF NOT (`a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 28(10) (src:843-845)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 28(10) the steps the relevant person must take in relation to A` MEANS
    LIST "verify that A is authorised to act on the customer's behalf", "identify A", "verify A's identity on the basis of documents or information in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of both A and the customer"

-- reg 28(11).  The relevant person must conduct ongoing monitoring of a business relationship, including (a) scrutiny of transactions undertaken throughout
-- the course of the relationship (including, where necessary, the source of funds) to ensure that the transactions are consistent with the relevant person's
-- knowledge of the customer, the customer's business and risk profile; (b) undertaking reviews of existing records and keeping the documents or
-- information obtained for the purpose of applying customer due diligence measures up-to-date.
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking): the keel's regulation 4 answers whether there is a business relationship.
-- src:846 | (11) The relevant person must conduct ongoing monitoring of a business relationship, including—
-- src:847 | (a) scrutiny of transactions undertaken throughout the course of the relationship (including, where necessary, the source of funds) to ensure that the transactions are consistent with the relevant person's knowledge of the customer, the customer's business and risk profile;
-- src:848 | (b) undertaking reviews of existing records and keeping the documents or information obtained for the purpose of applying customer due diligence measures up-to-date.
@ref reg 28(11) (src:846-848)
GIVEN `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(11) the relevant person must conduct ongoing monitoring of a business relationship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies when a relevant person is required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 28(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF NOT (`reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 28(11) (src:847-848)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 28(11) what ongoing monitoring includes` MEANS
    LIST "scrutiny of transactions undertaken throughout the course of the relationship (including, where necessary, the source of funds) to ensure that the transactions are consistent with the relevant person's knowledge of the customer, the customer's business and risk profile", "undertaking reviews of existing records and keeping the documents or information obtained for the purpose of applying customer due diligence measures up-to-date"

-- reg 28(12).  The ways in which a relevant person complies with the requirement to take customer due diligence measures, and the extent of the measures
-- taken (a) must reflect (i) the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1); (ii) its assessment of the level of risk arising in any particular case;
-- (b) may differ from case to case.
-- src:849 | (12) The ways in which a relevant person complies with the requirement to take customer due diligence measures, and the extent of the measures taken—
-- src:850 | (a) must reflect—
-- src:851 | (i) the risk assessment carried out by the relevant person under regulation 18(1);
-- src:852 | (ii) its assessment of the level of risk arising in any particular case;
-- src:853 | (b) may differ from case to case.
@ref reg 28(12) (src:849-853)
GIVEN `the ways and extent of the measures reflect the risk assessment carried out by the relevant person under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ways and extent of the measures reflect its assessment of the level of risk arising in any particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(12)(a) the ways and extent of the measures reflect what sub-paragraph (a) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the ways and extent of the measures reflect the risk assessment carried out by the relevant person under regulation 18(1)` AND `the ways and extent of the measures reflect its assessment of the level of risk arising in any particular case` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The ways in which a relevant person complies with the requirement to take customer due diligence measures, and the extent of the measures taken, must reflect—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- src:853 | (b) may differ from case to case.
@ref reg 28(12)(b) (src:853-853)
GIVEN `the ways and extent of the measures differ from case to case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(12)(b) the ways and extent of the measures may differ from case to case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the ways and extent of the measures differ from case to case` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sub-paragraph (b) says the ways and extent "may differ from case to case"; it does not say they must

-- reg 28(13).  In assessing the level of risk in a particular case, the relevant person must take account of factors including, among other things,
-- (a) the purpose of an account, transaction or business relationship; (b) the level of assets to be deposited by a customer or the size of the transactions
-- undertaken by the customer; (c) the regularity and duration of the business relationship.
-- src:854 | (13) In assessing the level of risk in a particular case, the relevant person must take account of factors including, among other things—
-- src:855 | (a) the purpose of an account, transaction or business relationship;
-- src:856 | (b) the level of assets to be deposited by a customer or the size of the transactions undertaken by the customer;
-- src:857 | (c) the regularity and duration of the business relationship.
@ref reg 28(13) (src:854-857)
GIVEN `it has taken account of the purpose of an account, transaction or business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the level of assets to be deposited by a customer or the size of the transactions undertaken by the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the regularity and duration of the business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(13) the relevant person has taken account of what paragraph (13) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken account of the purpose of an account, transaction or business relationship` AND `it has taken account of the level of assets to be deposited by a customer or the size of the transactions undertaken by the customer` AND `it has taken account of the regularity and duration of the business relationship` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person must take account of factors including, among other things—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

§ `Regulation 28(14) to (19) -- Discontinuing, demonstrating and verifying`

-- reg 28(15).  This paragraph applies if all the following conditions are met (a) a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation
-- to a customer; (b) the relevant person makes a disclosure required by (i) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000, or (ii) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime
-- Act 2002; and (c) continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the
-- relevant person under (i) section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 (tipping off: regulated sector); or (ii) section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.
-- src:859 | (15) This paragraph applies if all the following conditions are met—
-- src:860 | (a) a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation to a customer;
-- src:861 | (b) the relevant person makes a disclosure required by—
-- src:862 | (i) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 , or
-- src:863 | (ii) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 ; and
-- src:864 | (c) continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the relevant person under—
-- src:865 | (i) section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 (tipping off: regulated sector) ; or
-- src:866 | (ii) section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (tipping off: regulated sector) .
@ref reg 28(15) (src:859-866)
GIVEN `a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation to a customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person makes a disclosure required by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the relevant person under section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 or section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(15) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation to a customer` AND `the relevant person makes a disclosure required by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` AND `continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the relevant person under section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 or section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies if all the following conditions are met" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 28(14).  If paragraph (15) applies, a relevant person is not required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (2) or (10)
-- in respect of a customer.
-- src:858 | (14) If paragraph (15) applies, a relevant person is not required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (2) or (10) in respect of a customer.
@ref reg 28(14) (src:858-858)
GIVEN `reg 28(15) this paragraph applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(14) the relevant person is required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (2) or (10)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 28(15) this paragraph applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person is not required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (2) or (10)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If paragraph (15) applies"; the paragraph says nothing when paragraph (15) does not apply (exception polarity, fork F-polarity: the function asks the question the exception answers no to, so an unmet condition leaves that question to the rest of the Regulations)

-- reg 28(17).  Paragraph (16) does not apply to the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings.
-- src:870 | (17) Paragraph (16) does not apply to the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings.
@ref reg 28(17) (src:870-870)
GIVEN `the relevant person is the National Savings Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is the Director of Savings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(17) paragraph (16) does not apply to the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person is the National Savings Bank` OR `the relevant person is the Director of Savings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings"; the paragraph says nothing of another person (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 28(16).  The relevant person must be able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy its
-- requirements under this regulation are appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing, including risks (a) identified by
-- the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1); (b) identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to the relevant
-- person under regulations 17(9) and 47.
-- src:867 | (16) The relevant person must be able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy its requirements under this regulation are appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing, including risks—
-- src:868 | (a) identified by the risk assessment carried out by the relevant person under regulation 18(1);
-- src:869 | (b) identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47.
@ref reg 28(16) (src:867-869)
GIVEN `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (17) disapplies paragraph (16): the relevant person is the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(16) the relevant person is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures is appropriate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraph (17) disapplies paragraph (16): the relevant person is the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "paragraph (17) disapplies paragraph (16): the relevant person is the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings"
        IF `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1)` AND `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person must be able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken ... are appropriate" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 28(18)(a).  For the purposes of this regulation, except in paragraph (10), "verify" means verify on the basis of documents or information in either
-- case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified.
-- src:871 | (18) For the purposes of this regulation—
-- src:872 | (a) except in paragraph (10), “verify” means verify on the basis of documents or information in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified;
@ref reg 28(18)(a) (src:871-872)
GIVEN `the documents or information are obtained from a reliable source` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that source is independent of the person whose identity is being verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(18)(a) the identity is verified` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the documents or information are obtained from a reliable source` AND `that source is independent of the person whose identity is being verified` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“verify” means verify on the basis of documents or information in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified"

-- reg 28(18)(b).  Documents issued or made available by an official body are to be regarded as being independent of a person even if they are provided
-- or made available to the relevant person by or on behalf of that person.
-- src:873 | (b) documents issued or made available by an official body are to be regarded as being independent of a person even if they are provided or made available to the relevant person by or on behalf of that person.
@ref reg 28(18)(b) (src:873-873)
GIVEN `the documents are issued or made available by an official body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(18)(b) the documents are to be regarded as independent of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the documents are issued or made available by an official body` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Documents issued or made available by an official body"; the paragraph says nothing of other documents

-- reg 28(19).  Information may be regarded as obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified where
-- (a) it is obtained by means of an electronic identification process, including by using electronic identification means or by using a trust service
-- (within the meanings of those terms in Regulation (EU) No 910/2014); and (b) that process is secure from fraud and misuse and capable of providing
-- assurance that the person claiming a particular identity is in fact the person with that identity, to a degree that is necessary for effectively
-- managing and mitigating any risks of money laundering and terrorist financing.
-- src:874 | (19) For the purposes of this regulation, information may be regarded as obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified where—
-- src:875 | (a) it is obtained by means of an electronic identification process, including by using electronic identification means or by using a trust service (within the meanings of those terms in Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23rd July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market ); and
-- src:876 | (b) that process is secure from fraud and misuse and capable of providing assurance that the person claiming a particular identity is in fact the person with that identity, to a degree that is necessary for effectively managing and mitigating any risks of money laundering and terrorist financing.
@ref reg 28(19) (src:874-876)
GIVEN `it is obtained by means of an electronic identification process, including by using electronic identification means or by using a trust service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that process is secure from fraud and misuse and capable of providing assurance that the person claiming a particular identity is in fact the person with that identity, to a degree that is necessary for effectively managing and mitigating any risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 28(19) the information may be regarded as obtained from a reliable source independent of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is obtained by means of an electronic identification process, including by using electronic identification means or by using a trust service` AND `that process is secure from fraud and misuse and capable of providing assurance that the person claiming a particular identity is in fact the person with that identity, to a degree that is necessary for effectively managing and mitigating any risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be regarded as obtained from a reliable source which is independent ... where (a) ...; and (b) ..."; the paragraph says nothing of information obtained otherwise (Ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)
